    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσεράκοντα</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ρᾰ]</span>, 
			Ion.
		 and Hellenistic for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσαράκοντα</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.166
		</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
			<u>BMus.Inscr.</u>
			1005
		</span></i> (Cyzicus, <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
			<u>OGI</u>
			214.53
		</span></i> (Didyma, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), etc.; similarly <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσερακονταεννέα</span></b> , etc., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>forty-nine</i>, etc., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				10.1140.21
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, etc.; but also 
				Ion.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσαράϟ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οντα</span></span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Schwyzer</u>
				707
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				8
			</span></i> (Ephesus, <span class="entity">vi B.C.</span>); in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> some codd. usually have this form.</div>
